course: dictionary
lesson: 2480
title: One word, two meanings: daylight
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Daylight is a noun for the natural light of the Sun during the day: «Research suggests time outdoors in daylight lowers the risk of children becoming short-sighted.» Here daylight means the Sun's light, so you can be outside in it.
explain: Daylight can also mean dawn, the time when it first gets light: «We left before daylight.» How do you know? The word before tells you it was still dark, so daylight means the start of the day.
explain: Context shows you which meaning fits. Swap your meaning into the sentence: "We left before the Sun's light" sounds wrong, but "We left before dawn" works, so the second meaning is right.
fact: Daylight means the natural light of the Sun during the day.
fact: Daylight can also mean dawn, the time when it first gets light.
fact: «In broad daylight» means openly, in the full light of day, when everyone can see.
fact: Days have more daylight in summer and less in winter because of the Earth's tilt.
fact: Daylight is uncountable, so we say some daylight or more daylight, not a daylight.
exercise: «Research suggests time outdoors in daylight lowers the risk of children becoming short-sighted.» What does daylight mean in this sentence? | *The natural light of the Sun during the day | A bright lamp in the classroom | The time when it first gets light | A type of school timetable
exercise: «We left before daylight.» What does daylight mean here? | Daylight saving time | *Dawn, the time when it first gets light | Bright clothes for walking | The natural light of the Sun at noon
exercise: Mum says, «Walk home in daylight when possible.» What does she mean? | Walk home with a torch in the dark | Walk home only at midnight | *Walk home while it is light, when the Sun is up | Walk home without shoes
test: The Arctic tern follows the summer from the Arctic to the Antarctic, so it sees more daylight than any other animal. What does daylight mean here? | Darkness in a cave | A kind of clock that moves forward | Dawn, the first light of the morning | *The Sun's natural light during the day
test: «Walk a little way into a cave and the daylight disappears.» What disappears when you walk a little way into a cave? | Echoes | Your footprints | *Daylight | The water
exam: Which sentence uses daylight to mean dawn? | «Time outdoors in daylight helps protect children's eyes.» | «Walk a little way into a cave and the daylight disappears.» | *«We left before daylight.»
